# The guard's breach at 2026-11-25 17:49:21.807Z (void debug-kernel run 20261125-173057): root cause.
#
# Logged: "guard windows: gc573-pattern 1280x720+640+360 IsViewable", right after show.sh set DVI-D-0 to
# 1280x720@59.94. +640+360 is where SDL 2.30 creates ffplay's hidden 640x480 window: SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED,
# centred on display 0, the primary HDMI-0 1920x1200. show.sh's window-check.sh found the window at +1920+0 a
# moment later, and logged "player start (pid )", because the guard had removed the pid file meanwhile.
#
# Code (public sources, host versions: libsdl2 2.30.0+dfsg-1ubuntu3.1, ffmpeg 6.1.1-3ubuntu5):
# - ffplay 6.1.1 fftools/ffplay.c:3728 SDL_CreateWindow(..., SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED x2, 640, 480,
#   SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN | ...). video_open() (1321-1342), at the first frame: SetWindowTitle, SetWindowSize,
#   SetWindowPosition(-left, -top), ShowWindow, in that order.
# - SDL 2.30.0 src/video/x11/SDL_x11window.c X11_SetWindowPosition (787-845): XMoveWindow, then XSync, and a
#   wait until the X server reports the new position. X11_ShowWindow (1155-1182): XMapRaised, waiting for the
#   MapNotify. One connection, so the X server moves the window before it maps it. Nothing else in SDL moves
#   a window that is not fullscreen.
#
# Experiment, on gc573-dev's own display only (Xfce on Virtual-1 1280x800, the same SDL and ffmpeg packages;
# the user's screen untouched): 200 ffplay starts with show.sh's window options (override-redirect, -noborder,
# -left 0 -top 0 -x 1280 -y 720, title gc573-pattern), each shown for 0.2 s. SDL creates the window at
# 640x480+320+160 there. Two watchers ran side by side:
# - tools/testsrc/xwatch.py: the X server's own CreateNotify, ConfigureNotify and MapNotify events, in
#   order, with geometry;
# - guard.py's poll as it was then: `xwininfo -root -tree` for the geometry, then `xwininfo -id` for the map
#   state, every 50 ms.
#
# Result: the window was never mapped anywhere but its target. The breach was the poll's own artefact. Its
# tree query caught the window in the ~7 ms it sits resized at the creation position, unmapped. Its second
# query, after the move and the map, read "IsViewable". It paired the two.
#
# Fix (commit with this log):
# - guard.py watches windows by these X events (xwatch.py), not by polling.
# - ffplay runs with tools/testsrc/place.so, so the window never sits on the primary output, not even
#   hidden. The window is created at its final geometry. It is mapped only after a check under a server
#   grab: override-redirect, at that geometry, inside OUTPUT's RandR monitor, overlapping no other.
#
